              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "(a) Rufous-necked hornbill"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.089,
            0.633,
            0.111
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12.4 The Need for Classification"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.113,
            0.89,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Imagine walking into a huge library where thousands of books are scattered all over the floor. You want to read the book, On the Origin of Species by Charles Darwin. Where would you begin? Without arranging books into subjects, authors, or sections, finding any book would be difficult. In the same way, the Earth is home to millions of organisms. Therefore, classifying these organisms systematically helps us in understanding them better."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.24,
            0.613,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 12.2: Let us read a case study",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.261,
            0.75,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carefully read the given case study of Pakke Tiger Reserve."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.02,
            0.298,
            0.214,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.02,
                0.298,
                0.214,
                0.416
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.058,
                0.421,
                0.181,
                0.45
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "(b) Oriental Pied hornbill"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.28,
            0.89,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Pakke Tiger Reserve in Arunachal Pradesh is a forest where scientists have recorded nearly 300 bird species, which is striking given that India as a whole has about 1,300 bird species. Pakke is also known for supporting four species of hornbills — the Rufous-necked Hornbill, the Oriental Pied Hornbill, the Great Hornbill, and the Wreathed Hornbill (Fig. 12.3). These large birds nest only in large, old trees with suitable cavities and feed on specific fruits. As a result, different hornbill species are found in different parts of the forest depending on tree size and fruit availability. Studying such patterns allows scientists to ask precise questions about biodiversity, such as —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.051,
            0.463,
            0.202,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.051,
                0.463,
                0.202,
                0.635
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.055,
                0.645,
                0.184,
                0.661
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "(c) Great hornbill"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.452,
            0.888,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y How are species distributed within a forest? Which plants and animals are closely linked?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.487,
            0.888,
            0.522
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y How does classifying the four hornbill species help us understand biodiversity?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.523,
            0.813,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and discuss the case based on the following questions —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.038,
            0.688,
            0.218,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.038,
                0.688,
                0.218,
                0.836
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.543,
            0.749,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) How can scientists keep track of so many species?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.261,
            0.561,
            0.888,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The four hornbills look similar in some ways. What features can help scientists distinguish them from one another?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.596,
            0.888,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) What would happen if the large, old trees disappeared from the forest?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.038,
            0.839,
            0.201,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d) Wreathed hornbill"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.035,
            0.86,
            0.205,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 12.3: Four different species of hornbill found in the Pakke Tiger Reserve"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.633,
            0.89,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Many organisms show similarities in their external features, internal structure (such as tissues and organs) and cellular organisation. To make the study of such vast diversity easier, scientists group organisms based on their similarities and/or differences. This grouping helps to organise information, understand relationships among organisms and study life in a systematic manner. This scientific system of grouping living organisms is known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "biological classification",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.754,
            0.787,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Biological classification helps us in various ways, such as —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.774,
            0.888,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. It makes the study of living organisms more organised and systematic."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.811,
            0.889,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. It helps us understand the similarities and differences among living beings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.847,
            0.888,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. It helps us understand how different organisms are related to one another and how they interact."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.883,
            0.888,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. It helps us in identifying and naming the newly discovered organisms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.903,
            0.889,
            0.938
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. It supports biodiversity conservation by identifying the organisms that are under the threat of extinction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.048,
            0.926,
            0.124,
